title: Shape, built in public
description: Shape's own board: how the tool is built, and canvases inside it for what beta testers told us, the plan, the data and the numbers. Every feature of Shape is used somewhere here.
type: project
direction: right
routing: orthogonal
theme: brand

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the system
# shapes, colours, details, tags, links, sections, every kind of arrow

owner: Owner [person, detail: deyan]
tester: Beta testers [person, teal]
ai: Your AI CLI [cloud, purple, detail: Claude Code · Codex · Gemini, link: https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code, tags: tech]
pages: GitHub Pages [cloud, detail: dobrinov.github.io/shape]
note: Every change is an op:\nthe editor, the CLI,\nthe AI and undo use them [sticky, link: #core]
mermaid: Mermaid import [document, gray, detail: one way in, tags: legacy]
file: board.shape [parallelogram, detail: plain text in git]
status: 130 Rust tests · 27 browser tests [text, green]

group local: On your machine [gray] {
  window: Native window [rounded, detail: wry · tao, tags: tech]
  editor: Web editor [hexagon, detail: editor.js · no build]
}
group crates: Rust crates [blue] {
  cli: shape CLI [detail: server · exports · skills, tags: tech]
  group engine: shape-core [purple] {
    core: Model, DSL & ops [detail: the only way to change a board, link: #data-link]
    valid: Op valid? [diamond, orange]
    rejected: Rejected: nothing changes [text, red]
  }
  group outputs: Outputs [teal] {
    render: Layout & render [pill]
    prompt: Prompts [detail: outlines, not coordinates]
  }
  wasm: shape-wasm [cylinder]
  npm: @dobrinov/shape [cylinder, #d1495b]
}

owner -> window: opens a board
window -> editor: hosts [thick]
editor -> cli: /api/file · /api/git · /api/ai
cli -> core: apply ops
core -> valid
valid -> file: yes
valid -> rejected: no [red]
cli -> render, prompt
cli ..> ai: prompt on stdin
ai ..> prompt
render -> pages: the site's pictures
prompt => tester: ⌘⇧C spec
mermaid -- core: read by [dotted]
wasm <-> npm: same API [dashed]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the way into the canvases
# a box with `canvas:` opens a board inside this one; its shape is how the link looks

group inside: Inside this board [gray] {
  discovery-link: Discovery [pill, blue, canvas: discovery]
  plan-link: Roadmap [canvas: plan, detail: gantt · kanban · risks · decisions]
  data-link: Data & flows [text, canvas: data]
  metrics-link: Metrics [sticky, yellow, canvas: metrics]
  ai-flow-link: An AI edit, step by step [rounded, purple, canvas: data]
  screens-link: Shape's screens [rounded, teal, canvas: screens]
}

discovery-link -> plan-link -> data-link

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- review
comment on core by deyan: Should the schema block live in shape-core or its own crate?
reply c1 by claude: Its own crate (schema-core), plugged in as a block type; shape-core stays app-free.
comment on cli->ai by deyan: What if the AI CLI isn't signed in?
comment c3 at 40,-60 by deyan: Add the Homebrew tap to this picture
comment on mermaid by tester: Can I paste Mermaid into the editor? [resolved, resolution: "Yes: paste it and it becomes boxes and arrows"]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the board as slides
presentation: Shape in five minutes [instructions: "For a beta tester's first call: what it is, what's next"] {
  * [title: How Shape is built, notes: "Start here: one Rust core, a web editor, your own AI"]
  crates [title: The core, notes: "Every change is an op, and the DSL round-trips exactly"]
  discovery-link [title: What testers told us, transition: zoom]
  plan-link [title: What's next, notes: The schema block is next]
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- perspectives
perspective contributors: Contributors [tags: tech, show: adr sequence entity]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- a theme of our own
theme brand {
  font: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif
  radius: 10
  blue: #3b6fd8
  light {
    background: #f7f8fa
    section: #eef2f8
  }
  dark {
    background: #0f1318
    section: #161c24
  }
}

# ================================================================ canvases

canvas discovery: Discovery {
  # what beta testers told us, and the next task for the coding agent, as a prompt mindmap
  direction: right

  quote: "Z should be a magnifier for zooming in and out" — beta tester [sticky, yellow]
  sketch: The first board [image: wire, w: 248, h: 178]
  shipped: All six notes shipped in v0.59.0 [text, green]

  mindmap task: Bring ../schema onto the board as a block [layout: both] {
    Context
      ../schema draws Postgres schemas (crate schema-core)
      Shape already has entity blocks
      Database tables are drawn by hand today [link: #data-link]
    Goal
      A schema file opens as a block on the board
      Its tables update when the schema changes
    Constraints [red]
      shape-core stays free of app concerns
      The DSL round-trips exactly
      Few tokens: the AI reads tables, not coordinates
    Steps
      schema-core as an optional dependency
      A schema block that points at a file
      Render it like ../schema does
    Acceptance [green]
      structure.sql opens as a block
      A migration shows as a diff in review
    Open questions [collapsed]
      Rails schema.rb too?
      Edit the schema from the board?
  }

  mindmap beta: Beta notes [layout: down] {
    Asked for [blue]
      Resize a box from its corner
      Click a dot to add a box
      Z for a magnifier
    Felt wrong [red]
      Dragging stuttered
      The connector started at the centre
      The Dock said "exec"
    Shipped [green]
      All of it, in v0.59.0
  }

  quote ..> z-for-a-magnifier

  comment on quote by deyan: Same as Figma's Z: easy to remember

  canvas notes: All beta notes {
    layout: grid

    n1: Resize a card from its corner [sticky, green]
    n2: Dragging an image stutters [sticky, red]
    n3: Click a dot: a new box on that side [sticky, blue]
    n4: The window's icon says "exec" [sticky]
  }

  notes-link: Every note, as written [box, canvas: notes]

  asset wire: data:image/png;base64,
}

canvas plan: Roadmap {
  # when, what's in progress, what could go wrong, and why we chose what we chose

  gantt next: Next releases [start: 2026-10-20, scale: week] {
    Schema block design [3d, owner: deyan]
    Schema block [2w, after: schema-block-design, done: 10%]
    Linux window [1w, after: schema-block-design, purple]
    Beta round 2 [1w, after: schema-block, orange]
    v1.0 [after: beta-round-2 linux-window, milestone, green]
  }

  gantt outreach: Outreach [start: 2026-10-26, scale: week] {
    npm package [1w]
    Announcement [after: next/v1-0, milestone]
  }

  todo release: Release checklist {
    [x] Bump Cargo.toml and js/package.json [owner: claude]
    [x] Add a CHANGELOG entry [owner: claude]
    [ ] Commit and tag vX.Y.Z [owner: claude]
    [ ] Push, at most three tags at a time [owner: deyan]
      [ ] Check a Release run started for each
      [ ] Check the site deployed
    [ ] Update the Homebrew tap [owner: claude, due: 2026-10-20]
  }

  kanban work: Now {
    column todo: To do {
      schema: Schema block [owner: deyan]
      winconsole: Windows without a console window [detail: the binary opens a terminal today]
    }
    column doing: Doing {
      landing: Landing page tells Shape's own story [blue, owner: claude, link: #v1-0]
    }
    column review: In review {
      beta: Beta notes (v0.59.0)
    }
    column blocked: Blocked {
      linux: Linux window [orange, owner: deyan, detail: needs WebKitGTK on the build machines]
    }
    column done: Done {
      todos: To-do lists (v0.58.0) [green]
    }
  }

  risks project: Risks {
    Too many tags in one push [p: 3, i: 3, owner: deyan, detail: "GitHub skipped the builds when 7 tags went at once (2026-10-18)"]
    AI CLIs change their flags [p: 3, i: 4]
    Scope creep [p: 3, i: 5, detail: "The earlier attempt was dropped for being too complex"]
    Big boards get slow [p: 2, i: 3, owner: claude]
    Unknown unknowns
  }

  adr git: Git is the database [accepted] {
    context: Boards should diff, review and merge like code, with nothing new to host.
    options: A sync server; Files in git
    decision: A board is one text file; collaboration is commits and pull requests.
    consequences: No live cursors; merges go element by element instead.
  }

  adr own-ai: Use the user's own AI subscription [accepted] {
    context: People already pay for Claude, ChatGPT or Gemini.
    decision: Pipe the prompt to the CLI they're signed into; no API keys.
  }

  adr local: Run a local model [superseded] {
    decision: No local models for now (owner's call).
  }

  adr npm: Publish @dobrinov/shape to npm [proposed] {
    context: The package is built and tested in js/, but not on npm yet.
    options: Publish with each release; Wait for v1.0
  }

  adr rename: Rename diagram to Shape [accepted] {
    context: One name for the product, the command and the files.
    decision: shape, .shape and dobrinov/shape; the old names keep working.
  }

  table raci: Who does what {
    task      | owner | Claude Code | testers
    Discovery | A     | C           | R
    Build     | A     | R           | I
    Release   | R     | R           | I [green]
  }

  table options: Where the AI runs {
    option          | cost              | setup        | notes
    Your AI CLI     | your plan         | signed in    | What Shape does
    API keys        | pay per token     | a key each   | A second bill [red]
  }

  timeline history: How we got here {
    2026-10-07: v0.1: boards as text, comments as prompts [important]
    2026-10-11: The restart: mindmaps first (v0.2) [detail: an earlier, bigger attempt was dropped]
    2026-10-12: Gantt, charts, tables and themes [blue]
    2026-10-13: Kanban, decisions and sequence diagrams
    2026-10-15: Boards inside boards, merging, binaries for every OS
    2026-10-17: Rethink and the AI button
    2026-10-18: Perspectives, slides, a native window, wireframes; diagram becomes Shape [important, link: #rename]
    2026-10-19: To-do lists and the beta notes [green]
  }

  local -> own-ai: superseded by

  comment on beta-round-2 by deyan: Do we need more testers first?
}

canvas data: Data & flows {
  # Shape's own model as an ER diagram (its tables from model.sql), an AI edit as a sequence, a release in swimlanes

  schema model: Shape's model [file: model.sql] {
    entity boards {
      path:  text [pk]
      title: text
      theme: text [null]
    }
    entity nodes {
      id:     text [pk]
      board:  text [fk: boards, rel: drawn on]
      parent: text [null]
      label:  text [default: '']
    }
    entity edges {
      id:   text [pk]
      from: text [fk: nodes, rel: starts at]
      to:   text [fk: nodes, rel: ends at]
    }
  }
  entity comments: Comments {
    id [pk]
    on [fk: nodes]
    by
  }

  sequence edit: An AI edit {
    you: You [person]
    page: Editor
    server: Local server
    cli: Your AI CLI [cloud]
    you -> page: "Split Build into API and UI"
    page -> server: POST /api/ai
    server -> cli: prompt on stdin
    cli ..> server: a few ops
    server ..> page: ops
    page -> page: check the ops
    page ..> you: Keep or Discard
  }

  lanes release: A release {
    lane own: Owner {
      ask: Ask for a change [pill, green]
      push: Push it
    }
    lane claude: Claude Code {
      tested: Tests pass? [diamond]
      tag: Commit and tag
    }
    lane actions: GitHub Actions [blue] {
      build: Build every OS
      publish: Publish the release [pill]
    }
  }

  tap: Homebrew tap [cylinder]

  ask -> tested
  tested -> tag: yes
  tested -> ask: no
  tag -> push -> build -> publish
  publish ..> tap

  comment on tested: Which browser tests run on CI?

  cycle loop: The loop {
    Ask
    Build
    Release
    Hear back
  }
}

